===Etymology===
Cricket sense: origin disputed; supposedly from the belief that {{w|Horatio Nelson, 1st Viscount Nelson|Lord Nelson}} had one eye, one arm and one leg.

Wrestling sense: {{back-formation|en|full nelson}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-nelson.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[score]] of 111, sometimes considered to be [[unlucky]].
# {{lb|en|wrestling}} A [[wrestling]] [[hold]] in which a [[wrestler]]'s [[arm]] is [[locked]] behind their [[back]]. {{defdate|from late 19th c.}}

